# {{.ServiceName}}

Generated by `go-api new`. This is a starting point — the shapes it
generated ({{if .Resources}}the {{range $i, $r := .Resources}}{{if $i}}, {{end}}{{$r.Name}}{{end}} resource{{if gt (len .Resources) 1}}s{{end}}, {{end}}its store{{if .DB}}, its migrations{{end}}{{if .Authz}}, its Cedar policy{{end}}) are meant to be edited, not kept as-is.

## First run

```
go mod tidy   # resolves github.com/herlenashavi/go-api — needs network access
```
{{if .DB}}
Then apply the schema and run:

```
DATABASE_URL=postgres://... go run ./migrate up
DATABASE_URL=postgres://... DEBUG=true go run .
```
{{else}}
```
DEBUG=true go run .
```
{{end}}{{if eq .Authn "hmac"}}
`DEBUG=true` is what mounts `POST /dev/token` below — without it there's
no way to get a bearer token at all. Get one and call your API:

```
curl -X POST localhost:8080/dev/token -d '{"subject":"me","roles":["admin"]}'
# {"token":"..."}
curl localhost:8080/v1/{{if .Resources}}{{(index .Resources 0).Plural}}{{else}}your-resource{{end}} -H "Authorization: Bearer <token>"
```
{{end}}
## Configuration

Every env var `config.Base` reads (see `docs/config.md` in
github.com/herlenashavi/go-api) applies here. The ones this particular
service actually needs:

- `SERVICE_NAME` — defaults to `{{.ServiceName}}` if unset.
{{if .DB}}- `DATABASE_URL` — required; a `postgres://` connection string.
{{end}}{{if eq .Authn "hmac"}}- `DEV_JWT_SECRET` — signs/verifies dev tokens (see `authn.NewHMACVerifier`'s
  doc comment on why this is dev-only, never a production auth path).
{{end}}{{if eq .Authn "jwt"}}- `JWKS_URL`, `JWT_ISSUER`, `JWT_AUDIENCE` — required; this service verifies
  bearer tokens against a real JWKS endpoint.
{{end}}{{if .Authz}}- `POLICY_DIR` — defaults to `./policies`; edit `policies/{{.ServiceName}}.cedar`
  to change who can do what.
{{end}}
